0265-negroni-wlan-qrtr: Wi-Fi level 5 (negroniwlan=5), QRTR over the MHI IPCR channels 20/21.
New bsd/dev/negroni_wlan_qrtr.{c,h}: QRTR v1/v2 packet decoder with a bounds check on every length
(af_qrtr.c qrtr_endpoint_post rules), v1 encoder (src node 1, port CTRL / 0x4000), an 8 x 8 KiB RX
queue filled by the channel-21 callback and drained by negroni_wlan_qrtr_pump, RESUME_TX when the
chip sets confirm_rx, a server table from NEW_SERVER / DEL_SERVER, BYE handling.
Step 16 "QRTR HELLO": HELLO to node BCAST (node id still unknown, af_qrtr.c qrtr_hello_work) port
CTRL, wait for the chip's HELLO ("step 16 QRTR HELLO from node N"). Step 17 "WLFW service lookup":
wait for NEW_SERVER service 0x45 version 1, any instance ("step 17 WLFW service at node N port P").
Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0265".

